== room | NIGHT · MUSA'S ROOM | small bedroom at night with a laptop, a calculator and papers | phone
musa (worried): Quddus, I want to apply to eight universities. The application fees alone cost more than my rent.
quddus (talk): Have you checked if any of them offer an application fee waiver?
musa (shock): A what? You mean I can apply for free?
quddus (talk): Some universities waive the fee, for example for some international students, or for people who can't afford it. Not all, but it's worth checking.

== cafe | NEXT DAY · QUIET CAFÉ | quiet café with a laptop open and a cup of tea | cafe +laptop
musa (think): Where do I find it?
quddus (point): On the admissions page or the FAQ. Search for fee waiver. If it's not there, email admissions politely and ask.
> 1f4e9 | THE WAIVER EMAIL | 1f4cc Clear subject line | 1f393 The program you're applying to | 1f4b8 Short reason you need it | 1f4a1 Thank them for their time
musa (talk): And if they say no?
quddus (thumbs): Then you've lost nothing. Many people never ask, so they never get it.
musa (cheer): Eight emails sent. Polite, short, and no begging emojis!
